### 🟡 Medium — Missing negative / edge-case tests

These tests are **entirely absent**, leaving real bug vectors uncovered:

| # | Missing test | Risk |
|---|-------------|------|
| 11 | `UpdatePrice` on nonexistent SKU | Should throw `KeyNotFoundException` — never tested. |
| 12 | `GetProduct` for missing SKU | Should return `null` — never tested. |
| 13 | `ImportFromCsv` with malformed input | Will throw `IndexOutOfRangeException` or `FormatException` at L32-33 — no error handling exists and no test documents this. |
| 14 | `ApplyBulkDiscount` with 0%, 100%, or negative fractions | Edge-case math — never tested. |
| 15 | `ImportFromCsv` → `ExportToCsv` round-trip | Names containing commas will corrupt CSV — never tested. |

**Fix pattern:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
[ExpectedException(typeof(KeyNotFoundException))]
public void UpdatePrice_ThrowsWhenSkuNotFound()
{
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("MISSING", 5.00m);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetProduct_ReturnsNullForMissingSku()
{
    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("MISSING"));
}
```

