### Summary

| Severity | Count | Pattern |
|----------|-------|---------|
| 🔴 Critical | 6 | Method called, result discarded, zero assertions |
| 🟠 High | 4 | `Assert.IsNotNull` as only assertion (non-null ≠ correct) |
| 🟡 Medium | 5 | Missing negative/edge-case tests |

**Root cause:** Every test follows the same template — call the method, optionally check `IsNotNull`, call it done. This is the classic "coverage-touching" anti-pattern: line coverage reports look green because every code path *executes*, but no test actually verifies *behavior*. The suite would pass even if `Save` was a no-op, `UpdatePrice` doubled the price, or `Search` returned the entire catalog.
